 declared in the OpenAPI contract, matching its methods, paths, parameters, schemas, security, statuses, and behavior.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist application values, including derived and cached values, in PostgreSQL through the existing App connection string; preserve pre-existing database contents, initialize required structures safely, and retain committed values across requests and restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is true on a clean database, run App.Api/SeedData.cs at startup to populate each application table with two or three believable sample rows based on contract examples.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"When Seed:Demo is false at startup, skip demo seeding, insert no demo rows, and serve contract operations without requiring seeded records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Expose only backend API and documentation surfaces, with no product-facing screens or frontend implementation in the repository.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Calculate ingredient consumption and ration cost from as-fed weights, using dry-matter values only for nutritional calculations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Atomically reject feeding-event creations or corrections that require unavailable inventory without changing persisted event, inventory, movement, or lot rollup values; apply successful corrections as replacements of prior effects, and reverse a voided event’s inventory and rollup effects.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"When Days on Feed is zero, ADG is nonpositive, or no positive gain remains toward the target, return affected ADG, feed-to-gain metrics, and projected ship dates as unavailable when required positive denominators or gain are absent.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}